<br/>
<br/>There's 2 numbers listed, with PUF and NUF at the end of them. PUF stands for Personal Unholy Frenzy, and NUF stands for No Unholy Frenzy. <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=49016/unholy-frenzy">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_bladedarmor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unholy Frenzy</span></a> has been talked a lot through all of Wrath Classic, especially in regards to logs. Whether you use it on yourself or use it on another raider. <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=49016/unholy-frenzy">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_bladedarmor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unholy Frenzy</span></a> does snapshot <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=49028/dancing-rune-weapon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dancing Rune Weapon</span></a> - but that doesn't mean it's the best way to use it. If you're someone who only looks at damage meters, using it on yourself to make you look huge is a fine use. If you want to Parse and get your 99's and 100's - you're going to be using <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=49016/unholy-frenzy">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_bladedarmor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unholy Frenzy</span></a> on a <span class="c11">Feral Druid</span>. You probably should have been doing this before the buffs to Feral - but now with the buffs Feral is hands down the best target for <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=49016/unholy-frenzy">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_bladedarmor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unholy Frenzy</span></a>. Plus, that damage is now attributed to you in logs, allowing you to juice up your parses on the back of Ferals. Do as you wish, the choice is in your hands.<br/>
<br/>The above set is made for Trolls - in the event you're Alliance, remove one of the hit gems from the rings for a Strength gem.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems">Emblems of Frost for Blood Death Knight DPS in Phase 4</h3>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> become the new currency for phase 4. These emblems will hold their important for weeks after release, incentivizing people to play and do lower end content just to get these. In order to get the highest tier pieces, you'll need to first buy the tier with emblems which will require A LOT of them. You can earn 109 Emblems per week, except from the first week where you can only earn 105. 25 from each ICC raid size, 2 from each VoA raid size, 35 from Daily Heroic+++, 10 from the weekly raid, and 10 from the weekly ICC raid quest. <br/>
<br/>
<b>
<ins>Tier costs:</ins></b>
<br/>Helm: 95 <br/>Shoulders: 60<br/>Chest: 95<br/>Gloves: 60<br/>Pants: 95<br/>
<b>Total: 405</b>
<br/>
<br/>Some of these tier pieces won't be major upgrades over your 25-man Heroic ToGC loot - and their upgradability will be determined based on if you are able to get your hands on <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52025/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52028/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_judgementsofthejust.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a>. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52025/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> drops from ICC 10-man Heroic, and 25-man Normal. You need one of these marks to upgrade your emblem bought 251 ilvl tier to 264 Tier. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52028/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_judgementsofthejust.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> drop from only 25-man Heroic, and allows you to upgrade your 264 ilvl tier to 277 tier. <br/>
<br/>Due to the new nature of this path to tier, the list below may not be accurate for you. If you're able to upgrade a tier piece first, that would be my suggestion. The quicker you get to 4pc, the better. <br/>
